    closes: "The KDP window. main no longer prints a two-up page with one link for two puzzles, so the standing 'no book is to be generated for KDP' caveat is LIFTED."
    note: "Its BUILD gate was RED on the first run and GREEN on the second -- same commit 5c5d0aa, same database, same 8040 tests -- a non-deterministic uuid.UUID(hex=inf) read in a [db] test the card does not touch. Diagnosed to the app's module-global engine surviving conftest's DROP SCHEMA and filed as a backlog @ops item; it is the COST of this board's gate-condition change, unreachable while DATABASE_URL was unset. Both runs are recorded on the card and in suite-timing.log, because a gate green only on its second attempt is not the evidence a gate green on its first is. Review 8.5 found one important hole -- AC-6's horizontal refusal had no boundary and both its off-by-one mutants lived; a 7x10 book would have silently stopped pairing under one of them -- fixed in cycle 1, both mutants verified dead. The card's own '~2% tall-pair cost' was the orchestrator's arithmetic and was WRONG: the real figures are -4.95% for the worst surviving pair and outright refusal for 29..32-cell pairs. A second, horizontal refusal nobody had costed removes two-up pages entirely below ~6.913 in of trim, so 6x9 loses them. FR-040 amended at the architect station in the same window rather than deferred."
